}

tests {
  test("Status 201", function() { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
  test("has id", function() { expect(res.getBody().data).to.have.property("id"); });
  test("files is array", function() { expect(res.getBody().data.files).to.be.an("array"); });
}

docs {
  ## Create Documentation — POST /documentation

  All image/PDF/video fields are plain text URLs, not file attachments —
  upload to DigitalOcean Spaces first (`POST /api/v1/uploads/presigned-urls`),
  then send the resulting URLs here.

  Accepts **multipart/form-data** (what the mobile app sends — active body
  above) or **JSON** (switch the body mode to JSON in Bruno; same fields).
  In form-data, repeat the `files` field once per attachment (or send one
  `files` field holding a JSON array string); the type is taken from each
  URL's extension.

  Idempotent on `uuid` — retrying with the same uuid updates the existing
  report instead of creating a duplicate.

  `reportTypeId` must be offered in the project's state (see
  `GET /documentation/report-types?projectId=`), otherwise `400`.

  ### Request body

  | Field            | Type   | Required | Notes                                             |
  |------------------|--------|----------|---------------------------------------------------|
  | userId           | int    | no       | defaults to the logged-in user                    |
  | uuid             | string | no       | client-generated, for offline-sync dedup          |
  | projectId        | int    | yes      |                                                   |
  | institutionId    | int    | yes      | `institution.institute_id`                        |
  | reportTypeId     | int    | yes      |                                                   |
  | reportDate       | string | no       | `YYYY-MM-DD`, defaults to today                   |
  | remarks          | string | no       |                                                   |
  | hmLetterImage    | string | yes      | URL of the HM letter photo                        |
  | attachFeedback   | string | no       | URL of the feedback picture                       |
  | files            | array  | yes      | at least one additional image / PDF / MP4, in display order; form-data: repeat the field |
  | files[].url      | string | yes      | uploaded file URL (a plain URL string also works) |
  | files[].fileType | string | no       | `image`/`pdf`/`video` or a MIME type; else from the extension (pdf → pdf, mp4/mov/3gp/mkv/webm → video, anything else → image) |

  ### Response (201) — `data` object

  | Field            | Type     | Notes                                          |
  |------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
  | id               | int      |                                                |
  | uuid             | string   |                                                |
  | user_id          | int      |                                                |
  | full_name        | string   | submitting user                                |
  | emp_code         | string   |                                                |
  | project_id       | int      |                                                |
  | project_name     | string   | snapshotted at submit time                     |
  | state            | string   | the project's state                            |
  | institute_id     | int      |                                                |
  | institution_name | string   | snapshotted at submit time                     |
  | report_type_id   | int      |                                                |
  | report_type_name | string   | snapshotted at submit time                     |
  | report_date      | date     |                                                |
  | remarks          | string   |                                                |
  | hm_letter_image  | string   |                                                |
  | attach_feedback  | string   |                                                |
  | files            | array    | `[{ id, file_type, file_name, fullpath_url }]` |
  | is_active        | int      | `1`/`0`                                        |
  | created_at       | datetime |                                                |
  | updated_at       | datetime |                                                |
}
